# Where the troops of a Confederate command region were, for Official Records organization tables that list units
# under a district or department instead of a post. Used by pipeline/or_stations.py.
# pattern: regexes separated by ";" (case-insensitive) on a header (division/corps line) or the table heading
# scope:   optional regex the table heading must also match (blank = any)
# place|state: the region's headquarters town, located with data/places/geocoded.csv or GNIS ("Name@lat,lon" when GNIS has several)
# radius_km: how far the region's troops spread from it (drawn as the position's precision)
# Regions wider than ~120 km (a whole department or state) are left out on purpose: no position is better than a wrong one.
# dates:   optional 7th field "YYYY-MM-DD..YYYY-MM-DD": only tables dated in that window (field-army snapshots in camp or
#          winter quarters; the army's cavalry is not placed by these)
# who:     optional 8th field "cavalry": the line places only the army's cavalry and horse artillery (camps wider, apart)
# pattern|scope|place|state|radius_km|note|dates|who
Department of Richmond;Richmond Defenses;Department of Henrico||Richmond|VA|20|Richmond garrison (Elzey, Winder, Ransom)
